• **Today's three sessions did nothing:** the 00:17, 09:54 and 15:06 runs all show as `success`, but none of them produced any work. Every model call failed with HTTP 404. The cause is issue #962: a unit test, test_try_dispatch_subcommand_setup_bare, runs the real setup wizard in the repo root. It rewrote .yoyo.toml when an API key was in the environment, and the Day 210 safety commit 8a437178 saved that broken file.
• **Config fixed, cause still live:** Yuanhao fixed the config and the error detector (`13adf7cc`) and lowered `max_tokens` to 128000 (`331db0a7`). The test itself is still there and can do it again. A quick prompt through the binary now works on claude-opus-5-5.
• **A second test of the same kind:** `test_try_dispatch_subcommand_init_bare` calls the real `handle_init()`, which writes `YOYO.md` into the current directory. It is harmless here only because CLAUDE.md exists; in a checkout without it, cargo test would create a file. The fix for #962 should cover it too, plus a check of the other dispatch tests.
• **#961 (affects users):** the auto-check after each edit runs the full clippy + test chain even for `.md` or `.py` edits. That cost Day 207 its finished Task 1 when the task hit its time limit.
